---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Notice | Sofa Cleaning London"
  description="How Sofa Cleaning London handles the information you send us, what the quote form does with your details, and your rights under UK GDPR."
  noindex
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Privacy notice"
    lede="Plain English version: nothing is tracked unless you say yes to the cookie banner. The quote form itself collects nothing either way — it builds a message on your own phone and you decide whether to send it."
    trail={[{ href: '/privacy/', label: 'Privacy' }]}
  />

  <section class="container-page py-14 md:py-20">
    <article class="prose-body max-w-2xl">
      <h2 class="mt-0">What this website collects</h2>
      <p>
        By default, nothing that identifies you. We use <strong>Google Analytics (GA4)</strong> to
        understand how many people visit this site and which pages they read, but it is configured
        with Google Consent Mode so that it stores nothing on your device and sets no cookies
        until you accept the banner shown on your first visit. Declining, or simply not answering,
        means no cookie is ever written and no identifier is kept — the site works identically
        either way.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you accept, Analytics sets cookies so that repeat visits can be recognised as the same
        person, and the resulting data is processed by Google. We do not use it to advertise to
        you elsewhere, and we do not combine it with the details you send us through the quote
        form or WhatsApp.
      </p>
      <p>
        There is no advertising pixel and no other third-party tracking script on these pages,
        accepted or not.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your web host will also keep standard server logs, which typically include IP addresses
        and requested URLs, for security and diagnostics. That happens regardless of your cookie
        choice, is normal for any website, and is not used by us to identify or profile anyone.
      </p>

      <h2>What the quote form actually does</h2>
      <p>
        The quote form runs entirely in your browser. When you press the button it assembles the
        details you typed into a text message, shows that message to you, and then — only if you
        press the second button — opens WhatsApp with the text pre-filled.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing is submitted to this website, stored on a server, or emailed anywhere. You still
        press send inside WhatsApp yourself, and until you do, your details have not gone anywhere.
        If you close the page instead, nothing has been shared.
      </p>
      <p>
        Once you do send it, the message is handled by WhatsApp, which is operated by Meta under its
        own privacy terms. We receive it as an ordinary WhatsApp message on the business phone.
      </p>

      <h2>What we do with what you send us</h2>
      <p>
        We use the information you give us — your name, contact number, address or postcode, and
        what needs cleaning — for one purpose: to quote for the work and to carry it out. The lawful
        basis is performance of a contract, or the steps you ask us to take before entering one.
      </p>
      <p>
        Photographs you send us are used to prepare your quote. We will not publish a photograph of
        your home or your furniture anywhere — including the before-and-after gallery on this site —
        unless you have specifically agreed to it.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not sell your details, share them with marketing companies, or add you to a mailing
        list.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        If you accept the cookie banner, Google Analytics sets a small number of cookies to
        distinguish one visitor from another and to remember a session for up to 24 hours. None of
        them identify you personally, and none are used for advertising.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your choice is remembered in your browser, so you are only asked once. To change your
        mind later, clear this site's data in your browser settings and the banner will appear
        again on your next visit. You can also block Google Analytics outright by adjusting your
        browser's cookie settings or using a tracker-blocking extension — the site works
        identically either way, since nothing here depends on analytics to function.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Job records and invoices are kept for as long as UK tax and accounting rules require,
        currently six years. Message threads and quote enquiries that do not become bookings are
        deleted once they are clearly no longer relevant.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under UK GDPR you can ask us for a copy of the information we hold about you, ask us to
        correct it, ask us to delete it, or object to how we are using it. Email
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or call
        <a href={`tel:${site.phoneE164}`}>{site.phoneDisplay}</a> and we will deal with it within a
        month.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are not satisfied with how we have handled your information, you can complain to the
        Information Commissioner's Office, the UK supervisory authority for data protection.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} — <a href={`tel:${site.phoneE164}`}>{site.phoneDisplay}</a> or
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</Base>
